{{/if}}

What the overlay shows is Wick's, under Diagnostics below.

## The driver switches

Nine switches give a scenario a hold on the game's autonomous systems, so it
can watch one behavior without another arriving on top of it. Each is on when
the game is played, each is restored to on by `reset`, each is left as it
stands by `setScreen`, each is set by its own operation below, and each is
reported by the snapshot under the same name. A switch changes only what it
names; turning one back on resumes that faculty from the next tick, with no
catching up for the ticks it missed.

| Operation | Switch | While it is on | While it is off |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `setSpawning(on)` | `spawning` | The window spawn timer counts down and spawns as `specs/enemies.md` states. | The timer holds where it stands and no window spawn lands. |
| `setEvents(on)` | `events` | The scripted events fire on their exact tick. | No scripted event fires; an event whose tick passes while the switch is off never fires. |
| `setDespawning(on)` | `despawning` | Commons beyond `DESPAWN_DISTANCE` are removed. | Nothing is removed by distance. |
| `setEnemyMotion(on)` | `enemyMotion` | Every enemy moves as its behavior states, recomputing its heading where the behavior does. | Every enemy holds its position and heading. `age` and `contactCooldown` still count. |
| `setEnemyContact(on)` | `enemyContact` | An overlapping enemy whose cooldown is due hits. | No enemy hits. Every `contactCooldown` still counts down. |
| `setWeaponFire(on)` | `weaponFire` | Cooldown timers count down and due weapons fire or pulse. | Every cooldown timer holds where it stands and nothing fires or pulses. |
| `setEffectMotion(on)` | `effectMotion` | Projectiles integrate, lanterns revolve, shards bounce, and sconces decelerate. | Every projectile holds its position and velocity, and every lantern holds its angle. `ttl` and every re-hit entry still count, and hits still resolve. |
| `setDrops(on)` | `drops` | An enemy that dies leaves what `specs/world.md` gives it: a common's gem and the bread or draft its roll drops, and an elite's chest. | A death leaves nothing on the field and makes no drop roll, so a posed `nextDrop` stands. The enemy still dies, still counts as a kill, and still sounds. |
| `setProgression(on)` | `progression` | Experience gained is spent on levels as `specs/progression.md` states: `xp` falls by `xpToNext(level)`, `level` rises, and a level-up is queued. | No gain is spent: `xp` rises as gems are collected and stands however high it climbs, and `level` and `pendingLevelUps` hold where they are. |

The overlays are gated by neither `drops` nor `progression`: on every `playing`
tick, whatever the two hold, phase 12 of `specs/world.md` runs, so a tick that
collected a chest opens the chest overlay and a tick that ends with
`pendingLevelUps` above `0` opens the level-up overlay. Collection is gated by
neither either: a gem or a pickup already on the field is attracted and
collected as phases 8 and 9 state, and a collected gem's experience still
reaches `xp`.

Placement is gated by neither `weaponFire` nor `effectMotion`: on every
`playing` tick, whatever the two hold, the placement part of phase 5 of
`specs/world.md` runs, so the shapes that phase places are created, removed,
re-centered, and resized exactly as it states.

## The operations

The surface carries `version` (`WICK_DEBUG_VERSION`, `1`), a plain number, and
the operations below. Values are plain numbers, strings, booleans, and plain
objects. `x` and `y` are world units on the plane whose origin is where the run
began, every duration is in seconds, and `tick` is a whole count of ticks.

Each pose sets one thing and leaves the rest of the game as it stands, so a
caller that wants several things arranged makes several calls, in the order it
wants them. No pose decides an outcome: every hit, kill, drop, collection,
level-up, evolution, and ending comes from the ticks run after the pose, so a
scenario reads what happened from the snapshot.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}

Each operation's first parameter is the current state,
`DeepReadonly<WickState>`. A pose returns the next `WickState`, built from the
one it was handed, which it leaves as it was; a reading returns what it read.
The headings below name the parameters that follow the state.
{{/if}}

An argument outside the domain its operation states is invalid, and the call
throws rather than guessing what was meant; no operation rounds, clamps, or
otherwise normalizes an argument. A pose reaches the value it names whatever
the game's own rules would have allowed, and a value the game has no defined
state for makes the call fail loudly.

No operation asks how the caller got to it. The screen showing, the overlay
open, and what a player would have had to do first are the route a player takes
and are not an operation's conditions, so every operation below acts on the
game from wherever it stands: `setHp` sets the health on `title` as readily as
on `playing`, and `spawnEnemy` puts an enemy on the field whatever screen is
up. What no operation does is refuse quietly, returning with the state as it
was.

A pose changes the state alone and sounds nothing. A pose that creates an
entity gives it the next id from `nextId`, and a posed enemy, projectile,
puddle, gem, or pickup first moves, first hits, and first pulses on the next
tick, exactly as one a tick created.

### Core

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
#### `setAutoStep(auto)`

Takes the game off real time, and gives it back. `setAutoStep(false)` stops the
frame loop feeding the wall clock's delta time into the tick accumulator, so no
tick runs until `step` or `advance` runs one. `setAutoStep(true)` returns the
game to advancing itself, which is how a build starts and how it is played. It
changes no game state.

Drawing and input are unaffected either way: the build's own loop keeps running
frames in real time, each reading the keys, reconciling the loops, mirroring
`muted`, and rendering, so a menu still answers a key press while the
simulation is held. The snapshot reports the switch as `autoStep`, and `reset`
leaves it untouched.

#### `step(ticks)`

Runs `ticks` frames of the build's loop immediately and in order, whatever the
screen. `ticks` is a whole number of at least `1` and defaults to `1`. Each
frame is exactly a frame of the loop: it reads the keys as they stand, the held
movement values and the press edges, runs the screen's update, then renders.

On `playing` the update is one whole tick of `specs/world.md`, run directly
rather than through the accumulator, with the frame's held movement values
applied to that tick. The accumulator is left as it stands, except that a tick
which leaves `playing` discards it as any such tick does. On every other
screen the update ticks nothing: the menu edges are read, the loops are
reconciled, `muted` is mirrored, and `run.tick` is untouched. `simTime` rises
by `TICK_DT` per frame on every screen. A frame whose tick opens an overlay or
ends the run is followed by the remaining frames on the screen it opened, so
`step(n)` always runs `n` frames.

#### `advance(seconds)`

Runs one frame of the build's loop worth `seconds` of delta time, a real number
above `0`, exactly as a wall-clock frame of that length: the keys are read,
`simTime` rises by `seconds`, and on `playing` the delta joins the accumulator
and every whole `TICK_DT` in it is consumed as a tick, the remainder waiting in
`accumulator`. A tick that opens an overlay or ends the run is the last the
frame runs and the remainder is discarded. On any other screen the frame ticks
nothing and the accumulator stays `0`. Then a render. This is the operation
that poses a partial frame.

#### `reset()`
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `reset(state)`
{{else}}
#### `reset()`
{{/if}}

Restores every declared field of the game's state to its title-screen value:
the `title` screen with `menuIndex`, `almanacTab`, and `almanacScroll` all `0`,
the idle run of `specs/state.md`, the accumulator and `simTime` at `0`, and
every driver switch on. `muted` stays as it is.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
`autoStep` stays as it is: it belongs to the caller driving the game rather than
to the session being played, so a `reset` inside a stepped scenario leaves the
game off the wall clock. Any looping cue stops on the next frame, which
`step(1)` runs one of.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
Any looping cue stops on the next `update`, since the state it restores holds no
run.
{{else}}
Any looping cue stops on the next tick of the game mode, since the state it
restores holds no run.
{{/if}}

A reset leaves the game indistinguishable from a freshly started session, so
anything else the build keeps across frames is derived from what a reset
restores.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `snapshot(state)`

A pure reading of `state`, returned as the plain object under Snapshot shape
below. It returns no state, because it poses nothing.
{{else}}
#### `snapshot()`

A pure read of the state, returned as the plain object under Snapshot shape
below. It changes nothing.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `reconcile(state)`
{{else}}
#### `reconcile()`
{{/if}}

Brings every value this surface reports into agreement with the game as it now
stands, without advancing anything. `time`, `xpToNext`, `maxHp`, `armor`,
`moveSpeed`, `pickupRadius`, `spawnWindow`, `aliveCommons`, and `pool` all
follow from the run clock, the level, the passives held, the enemies on the
field, and the slots as they stand, so after a pose they answer for the run as
it is now rather than as it was before it.

A build that works those out at the read has nothing to do here and this call
changes nothing. A build that keeps any of them as a stored copy rewrites that
copy from what it is a copy of.

It moves no clock and runs no system: `run.tick`, `accumulator`, and `simTime`
are untouched, no enemy moves, no projectile integrates, no hit or kill
resolves, nothing is collected, no cooldown timer, `ttl`, `age`,
`contactCooldown`, `hurtFlash`, or `spawnTimer` counts down, no held key is
read, no random draw is made, and every posed outcome stands. It sounds no cue,
opens and closes no overlay, changes no screen, and queues no level-up. It
moves nothing to make a reading agree: an enemy posed on top of the lamplighter
stays where it was posed and reads as it is, and a health posed above `maxHp`
is not brought back under it. What the specification gives a later moment stays
there: the camera follows on the next render, the aura and the lanterns follow
on the next tick, and `nextOffers` is checked against the pool when the next
overlay opens.
`kills`, `xp`, and `firedEvents` are what the run has accumulated rather than
readings of the run as it stands, so they are the ticks' and this call leaves
them where they are. Calling it twice leaves the same state as calling it once.

It is never an error, whatever screen is showing and whether or not the
simulation is held.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}

`reconcile(state)` returns the next `WickState`, built from the one it was
handed, which it leaves as it was. A build that works every one of those
readings out at the call returns a state equal to the one it was given.
{{/if}}

### Screens

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setScreen(state, name)`
{{else}}
#### `setScreen(name)`
{{/if}}

Sets `screen` to `name`, one of the `Screen` values, with `menuIndex`,
`almanacTab`, and `almanacScroll` all `0`. Nothing else changes: the run, the
loadout, `offers`, `nextOffers`, `chestResult`, `pendingLevelUps`, every posed
outcome, `simTime`, and the driver switches all stand exactly as they were, and
no cue
sounds at the call. A call that leaves `playing` discards the accumulator, as
every frame and pose that leaves `playing` does.

The pose sets the screen and nothing else, so a run is never begun, discarded,
ended, or grown by it. What a screen shows is arranged before the pose or
reached through the game's own systems: a fresh run is `reset`, this pose to
`playing`, and `setWeapon(0, "taper", 1)`; the idle run the menus hold is
`reset`; the level-up overlay is `setPendingLevelUps` and one `playing` tick;
the chest overlay is `spawnPickup("chest", x, y)` at the lamplighter's center
and one tick, which is the real collection path; the fallen ending is `setHp`
at `0` and one tick; and the dawn ending is `setTick` at
`DAWN_TIME × TICK_HZ − 1` (`35999`) and one tick.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `choose(state, index)`
{{else}}
#### `choose(index)`
{{/if}}

Accepts the offer at `index`, counted from `0` down the list, exactly as moving
the highlight there and pressing `confirm` would: the item is applied,
`pendingLevelUps` falls by one, and either the next queued overlay opens with a
fresh pool or `screen` returns to `playing`. It carries out that acceptance
from wherever the game stands, `levelup` showing being how a player reaches the
choice rather than a condition on the call. `index` is a whole number naming an
offer of `offers`; an `index` outside that list, a negative one included, names
no offer, so the call fails loudly, as it does whenever `offers` is empty.
Sounds nothing.

### Menus

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `menuRects(state)`
{{else}}
#### `menuRects()`
{{/if}}

Reports the rectangles of the current screen's vertical menu, in menu order,
each a plain object carrying `x`, `y`, `width`, and `height` in stage
coordinates, `0` to `STAGE_W` across and `0` to `STAGE_H` down, which are the
coordinates the pointer is read in. `title`, `levelup`, `paused`, `fallen`, and
`dawn` report one rectangle per item of the menu they show. `almanac` reports
one rectangle per visible entry row, in list order from `almanacScroll` and at
most `ALMANAC_ROWS` of them, so a tab holding fewer entries than that reports
one per entry. `howto` and `chest` report exactly one rectangle, the area the
screen's way out is taken in. `playing` reports an empty list. Each rectangle is
the area a hover, a press and release, or a touch contact selects that item
inside, so what this reading reports is what the pointer and touch rules of
`specs/controls.md` act on.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
It returns no state, because it poses nothing.
{{else}}
It changes nothing.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `tabRects(state)`
{{else}}
#### `tabRects()`
{{/if}}

Reports the rectangles of the almanac's tab bar on `almanac`, one per tab in
`ALMANAC_TABS` order, each a plain object carrying `x`, `y`, `width`, and
`height` in the same stage coordinates. Every other screen reports an empty
list. Each rectangle is the area a press and release or a touch contact selects
that tab inside, and it meets no rectangle `menuRects` reports on that screen.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
It returns no state, because it poses nothing.
{{else}}
It changes nothing.
{{/if}}

### The driver switches

#### The nine switch operations

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
`setSpawning(state, on)`, `setEvents(state, on)`, `setDespawning(state, on)`,
`setEnemyMotion(state, on)`, `setEnemyContact(state, on)`,
`setWeaponFire(state, on)`, `setEffectMotion(state, on)`,
`setDrops(state, on)`, and `setProgression(state, on)` set the nine driver
switches, as The driver switches above describes.
{{else}}
`setSpawning(on)`, `setEvents(on)`, `setDespawning(on)`, `setEnemyMotion(on)`,
`setEnemyContact(on)`, `setWeaponFire(on)`, `setEffectMotion(on)`,
`setDrops(on)`, and `setProgression(on)` set the nine driver switches, as The
driver switches above describes.
{{/if}}
`on` is a boolean. Each applies on every screen and changes nothing but its
switch.

### The clock

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setTick(state, tick)`
{{else}}
#### `setTick(tick)`
{{/if}}

Sets `tick` to `tick`, a whole number from `0` to `DAWN_TIME × TICK_HZ − 1`
(`35999`). Nothing else changes: `spawnTimer`, `firedEvents`, and every live
entity stay as they stand, and everything derived from the clock, `time`,
`spawnWindow`, the health scaling of later spawns, and which event is due,
follows from the next tick on. A scripted event fires only on its exact tick,
so a clock posed past an event never fires it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setSpawnTimer(state, seconds)`
{{else}}
#### `setSpawnTimer(seconds)`
{{/if}}

Sets `spawnTimer` to `seconds`, at least `0`.

### Drawn outcomes

Where the game draws at random, each pose below sets what the next such draw
decides. Each value is held in the run under the name its snapshot field
carries, is `null` on the idle run and after the draw that consumed it, is left
standing by `setScreen`, and is consumed by one draw alone. A value that is not
valid at the moment its draw is made is discarded and the draw is made at
random. `rollDrop`, the one reading here, makes a drop roll on its own and
returns it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextSpawnAngle(state, degrees)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextSpawnAngle(degrees)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextSpawnAngle` to `degrees`, a real number of at least `0` and below
`360`, measured from `+x` toward `+y`; any other value is invalid. The next
spawn point the director draws, for a window spawn or for a scripted event
that spawns an enemy at a spawn point, is at that angle as `specs/enemies.md`
states, and that spawn consumes it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextSwarmAngle(state, degrees)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextSwarmAngle(degrees)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextSwarmAngle` to `degrees`, in the same domain. The next gnat swarm's
direction `d` is the unit vector at that angle, and that swarm consumes it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextSpawnType(state, id)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextSpawnType(id)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextSpawnType` to `id`, an enemy id of `specs/enemies.md`; any other
value is invalid. The next window spawn is of that type in place of the type
drawn from the window's types, and that spawn consumes it. A window spawn
whose row does not list the type discards it and draws at random. A scripted
event spawns what its row states and leaves it standing.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextPuddleOffset(state, dx, dy)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextPuddleOffset(dx, dy)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextPuddleOffset` to `(dx, dy)`, real numbers whose length is at most
`OIL_SCATTER` (`400`); a longer offset is invalid. One puddle of the next Oil
Splash or Blaze firing lands at the lamplighter's center of that tick plus the
offset, the firing's other puddles land at random, and that firing consumes
it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextStrikeTarget(state, id)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextStrikeTarget(id)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextStrikeTarget` to `id`, the id of a live enemy; any other value is
invalid. The first strike of the next Spark firing lands on that enemy when it
is alive and within `SPARK_RANGE` of the player's center on the tick of the
firing, the firing's other strikes are drawn from the other eligible enemies,
and that firing consumes it. A firing on which it is dead or out of range
discards it and draws every strike at random.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextChestItem(state, id)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextChestItem(id)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextChestItem` to `id`, a base weapon id or a passive id; any other
value is invalid. The next chest opened consumes it, whatever its result: when
rule 2 of `specs/evolutions.md` decides that chest, the item rises by one level
when it is held below its max level, and otherwise the chest draws at random.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextDrop(state, kind)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextDrop(kind)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextDrop` to `kind`, one of `bread`, `draft`, and `none`; any other
value is invalid. The next common enemy killed by a weapon while `drops` is on
drops that pickup beside its gem, or nothing for `none`, in place of its roll,
and that kill consumes it. A death while `drops` is off, an elite's death, and
the Dark's death leave it standing.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `rollDrop(state)`
{{else}}
#### `rollDrop()`
{{/if}}

Makes one drop roll exactly as `specs/world.md` states under The drop roll and
returns what it decided: `bread`, `draft`, or `none`. It is a reading of the
roll alone: nothing drops, nothing dies, no cue sounds, and every field of the
state stands as it was, `nextDrop` included, since a posed drop has no part in
it.

### The lamplighter

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setPlayerPosition(state, x, y)`
{{else}}
#### `setPlayerPosition(x, y)`
{{/if}}

Sets the lamplighter's center to `(x, y)`. Nothing else moves: the camera
follows on the next render, and the aura and lanterns follow on the next tick.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setFacing(state, facing)`
{{else}}
#### `setFacing(facing)`
{{/if}}

Sets `facing` to `facing`, `"left"` or `"right"`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setHp(state, hp)`
{{else}}
#### `setHp(hp)`
{{/if}}

Sets `hp` to `hp`, a real number, and there is no bound either way. `maxHp` is
worked out from the passives held and moves as they change, so it is what
ordinary play holds the health under rather than a limit on this pose: a value
above it is applied as it was given, and what the game's own recovery step then
makes of it is that step's answer. A value at or below `0` ends the run fallen
at the end of the next `playing` tick, through the ending rule of
`specs/world.md`.

### Progression

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setLevel(state, level)`
{{else}}
#### `setLevel(level)`
{{/if}}

Sets `level` to `level`, a whole number of at least `1`. `xp` is untouched.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setXp(state, xp)`
{{else}}
#### `setXp(xp)`
{{/if}}

Sets `xp` to `xp`, a real number of at least `0`. No level-up is derived from
it: a level-up comes from the next gain.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setKills(state, kills)`
{{else}}
#### `setKills(kills)`
{{/if}}

Sets `kills` to `kills`, a whole number of at least `0`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setPendingLevelUps(state, count)`
{{else}}
#### `setPendingLevelUps(count)`
{{/if}}

Sets `pendingLevelUps` to `count`, a whole number of at least `0`. A `playing`
tick that ends with it above `0` opens the overlay exactly as a gain does.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setNextOffers(state, ids)`
{{else}}
#### `setNextOffers(ids)`
{{/if}}

Sets `nextOffers` to `ids`, a list of `1` to `OFFER_COUNT` (`3`) distinct ids,
each a weapon id, base or evolved, a passive id, or `LAMP_OIL_ID`; a length
outside that range, a repeated id, or any other string is invalid. The list is
checked against the candidate pool at the moment the next level-up overlay
opens: it is accepted when every id is a candidate of the pool at that moment,
or when it holds `LAMP_OIL_ID` alone while the pool is empty, and the overlay
then presents exactly that list in that order. Otherwise it is discarded whole
and the overlay draws at random; an evolved weapon's id is never in a pool, so
a list naming one is always discarded. One overlay consumes it, and a later
overlay draws at random again. Called on `levelup`, the overlay the list is
checked against is the queued one.

### The loadout

`slot` counts from `0`. `weapons` and `passives` stay contiguous: a placement
in slot `weapons.length` appends, and a removal moves the slots after it up by
one.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setWeapon(state, slot, id, level)`
{{else}}
#### `setWeapon(slot, id, level)`
{{/if}}

Puts weapon `id`, a `WeaponId`, at `level` in `slot`. `slot` is `0` to
`weapons.length`, at most `WEAPON_SLOTS − 1`; `level` is `1` to
`MAX_WEAPON_LEVEL` for a base weapon and `1` for an evolved one. Invalid: an
`id` already held in another slot; a base weapon whose evolution is held in
another slot; an evolved weapon whose base is held in another slot. When the
slot's `id` changes its cooldown timer becomes `0`; when only the level changes
the timer keeps counting. Nothing else changes: the aura of Halo or Corona and
the lanterns of Chandelier appear on the next `playing` tick under the
placement rule.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setWeaponCooldown(state, slot, seconds)`
{{else}}
#### `setWeaponCooldown(slot, seconds)`
{{/if}}

Sets the cooldown timer of the weapon in `slot`, a held slot, to `seconds`, at
least `0`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `removeWeapon(state, slot)`
{{else}}
#### `removeWeapon(slot)`
{{/if}}

Removes the weapon in `slot`, a held slot. Its aura or lantern set is removed
on the next `playing` tick under the placement rule; the projectiles and other
zones it produced stay.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setPassive(state, slot, id, level)`
{{else}}
#### `setPassive(slot, id, level)`
{{/if}}

Puts passive `id`, a `PassiveId`, at `level` in `slot`. `slot` is `0` to
`passives.length`, at most `PASSIVE_SLOTS − 1`; `level` is `1` to the
passive's `maxLevel` in `PASSIVES`. An `id` held in another slot is invalid.
`hp` is untouched; `maxHp`, `armor`, `moveSpeed`, `pickupRadius`, and every
multiplier follow from the next read.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `removePassive(state, slot)`
{{else}}
#### `removePassive(slot)`
{{/if}}

Removes the passive in `slot`, a held slot. `hp` is capped at the new `maxHp`
on the next tick's recovery step.

### Enemies

An `id` that names no live enemy is invalid for every operation below that
takes one.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `spawnEnemy(state, type, x, y)`
{{else}}
#### `spawnEnemy(type, x, y)`
{{/if}}

Spawns one enemy of `type`, an `EnemyId`, centered at `(x, y)` through the real
spawn path: its `maxHp` is scaled by the run clock exactly as a director spawn
is, its `age` and `contactCooldown` are `0`, it takes the next id, and its
heading is the one `specs/enemies.md` gives a spawn at that point, the unit
vector toward the lamplighter's center, or the facing direction when the two
coincide.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setEnemyPosition(state, id, x, y)`
{{else}}
#### `setEnemyPosition(id, x, y)`
{{/if}}

Moves enemy `id` to `(x, y)`; its heading, age, and health are untouched. A
weaver's anchor follows from the new position.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setEnemyHp(state, id, hp)`
{{else}}
#### `setEnemyHp(id, hp)`
{{/if}}

Sets enemy `id`'s `hp` to `hp`, a real number above `0`; `0` and below are
invalid, since death is decided by the tick. There is no upper bound: an
enemy's `maxHp` is scaled by the run clock at its spawn, so it is what ordinary
play holds the enemy under rather than a limit on this pose, and a value above
it is applied as it was given.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setEnemyHeading(state, id, hx, hy)`
{{else}}
#### `setEnemyHeading(id, hx, hy)`
{{/if}}

Sets enemy `id`'s heading to the unit vector of `(hx, hy)`; a zero vector is
invalid. A chaser or weaver recomputes its heading on its next move, so this
poses a drifter.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setEnemyAge(state, id, seconds)`
{{else}}
#### `setEnemyAge(id, seconds)`
{{/if}}

Sets enemy `id`'s `age` to `seconds`, at least `0`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setEnemyContactCooldown(state, id, seconds)`
{{else}}
#### `setEnemyContactCooldown(id, seconds)`
{{/if}}

Sets enemy `id`'s `contactCooldown` to `seconds`, at least `0`.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `removeEnemy(state, id)`
{{else}}
#### `removeEnemy(id)`
{{/if}}

Removes enemy `id`. Nothing drops, nothing counts as a kill, and no cue plays.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `clearEnemies(state)`
{{else}}
#### `clearEnemies()`
{{/if}}

Removes every enemy, elites and the Dark included, the same way.

### Projectiles and zones

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `spawnProjectile(state, weapon, x, y, vx, vy, pierce)`
{{else}}
#### `spawnProjectile(weapon, x, y, vx, vy, pierce)`
{{/if}}

Adds one projectile of `weapon`, one of `ember`, `pin`, `shard`, `sconce`,
`beacon`, and `hail`, centered at `(x, y)` with velocity `(vx, vy)` in units
per second and `pierce` a whole number of at least `0` or `INFINITE_PIERCE`
(`-1`). Its figures are the ones the weapon would give a projectile fired on
this tick: `radius` is the weapon's table radius at the level held, or at level
`1` (an evolved weapon's fixed row) when the weapon is not held, times the
`areaMul` in force at the call; `damage` is that row's damage times the
`damageMul` in force at the call; `ttl` is that row's duration; `hits` is
empty. A `sconce` takes acceleration `−SCONCE_DECEL` along the unit vector of
`(vx, vy)`, so a zero velocity is invalid for `sconce`; every other weapon
takes `(0, 0)`. Its `weapon` decides its re-hit interval and the effect drawn
over it.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `clearProjectiles(state)`
{{else}}
#### `clearProjectiles()`
{{/if}}

Removes every projectile.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `spawnPuddle(state, weapon, x, y)`
{{else}}
#### `spawnPuddle(weapon, x, y)`
{{/if}}

Adds one zone of kind `puddle` for `weapon`, one of `oil-splash` and `blaze`,
centered at `(x, y)`: `radius` is the weapon's table radius at the level held,
or at level `1` (Blaze's fixed row) when the weapon is not held, times the
`areaMul` in force at the call; `damage` is that row's damage times the
`damageMul` in force at the call; `ttl` is that row's duration; `hits` is
empty. It pulses first on the next tick and every `OIL_PULSE` or `BLAZE_PULSE`
after.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `clearZones(state)`
{{else}}
#### `clearZones()`
{{/if}}

Removes every zone, the aura and the lanterns included. An aura or a Chandelier
lantern set whose weapon is still held is created again on the next `playing`
tick under the placement rule.

Slashes, strikes, bursts, lanterns, and auras are never posed directly: each is
created by holding its weapon through `setWeapon` and running the tick it fires
on, and `setWeaponCooldown(slot, 0)` makes that the next tick.

### Gems and pickups

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `spawnGem(state, tier, x, y)`
{{else}}
#### `spawnGem(tier, x, y)`
{{/if}}

Places one unattracted gem of `tier`, a `GemTier`, at `(x, y)` with the next
id.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `setGemAttracted(state, id, attracted)`
{{else}}
#### `setGemAttracted(id, attracted)`
{{/if}}

Sets gem `id`'s `attracted` to `attracted`, a boolean; an `id` that names no
gem is invalid.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `clearGems(state)`
{{else}}
#### `clearGems()`
{{/if}}

Removes every gem; no experience is gained.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `spawnPickup(state, kind, x, y)`
{{else}}
#### `spawnPickup(kind, x, y)`
{{/if}}

Places one pickup of `kind`, a `PickupKind`, at `(x, y)` with the next id.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
#### `clearPickups(state)`
{{else}}
#### `clearPickups()`
{{/if}}

Removes every pickup; nothing is collected.
{{#if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}

